1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Finally, let's learn how to make a pair of pants.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:08,099
First of all, you can use the internal multidirectional line tool

3
00:00:08,099 --> 00:00:12,000
to draw a line that we will use later to cut the internal line.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,800
In the process of drawing, press the Ctrl key and click to create a curve point.

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,000
Double click to complete the creation.

6
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,500
After the creation is finished, use the edit version tool to select this line.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,500
Right-click to select Cut.

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:33,500
After the simulation is started, you can see that there is no vermilion between the two panels.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Then we will continue to complete the pocket cloth.

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,500
Now we choose the edge of the pocket for this seam.

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:47,500
Here we right-click on this edge to select the panel outline expansion.

12
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:54,500
After selecting the panel outline expansion, we can set the width of the panel expansion.

13
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,500
In the side corner below,

14
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,500
we need to switch to Extend,

15
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:01,500
so that it can be expanded according to the original ratio.

16
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,500
After the expansion is completed, click OK.

17
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,500
Don't forget to select the internal line.

18
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:14,500
This internal line is what we will use to sew the pocket cloth later.

19
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,500
After the panel outline expansion,

20
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,500
there will be a gap between the pocket and the pants panel.

21
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,500
So here we set a negative 1 layer for the pocket.

22
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,500
Because its layer is smaller than the pants 0,

23
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,500
it will automatically fit in after we start the simulation.

24
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:35,500
After the pocket has been automatically simulated to the inside,

25
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:40,500
we need to fix the extended part of it on the pants,

26
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,500
that is, to sew with the pants.

27
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,500
So now we have to choose the free sewing tool,

28
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,500
because we haven't set the cut point yet,

29
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,500
so we use the free sewing tool directly.

30
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,500
Click, click.

31
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:52,500
After sewing,

32
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:56,500
we also sew the bottom here to the pants panel.

33
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:01,500
Now, because the side of our pants and pocket are also stacked together,

34
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:02,500
and then sewed,

35
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,500
so we change the type of sewing line to Turn,

36
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,500
so that it can prevent instability.

37
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,500
Including the sewing line above,

38
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,500
it is the same.

39
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,500
In fact, at this point,

40
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:17,500
in general, our pants shoes are made like this.

41
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:21,500
But if you are moving or doing some special actions,

42
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,500
you can see that it is hollow in the middle.

43
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,500
We can fill this pocket.

44
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,500
First of all, we copy and paste this pocket panel,

45
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:36,500
and cut it along the inner line created before.

46
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,500
Before we officially sew,

47
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:43,500
we can put the position of this panel first.

48
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,500
Put it almost outside the pocket,

49
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:50,500
and then we choose this inner line in the middle to cut.

50
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,500
After cutting the inner line,

51
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,500
we delete the excess part.

52
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:00,500
Now we move the pants to the very outside of this side.

53
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,500
In the 3D space,

54
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,500
we can start to sew after arranging the panel.

55
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:11,500
First, we sew the top and bottom of this side part.

56
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,500
Also sew to the top of the pants.

57
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:16,500
Don't forget to change the type of sewing line to Turn.

58
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:24,500
Then we sew to the top of the pants.

59
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,500
Also sew to the top of the pants.

60
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:32,500
Then we sew the opening of the side and the opening of the pants together.

61
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:42,500
Then the bottom of the side and the pocket of the pocket are sewed together.

62
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:46,500
After creating the model of the charger,

63
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,500
there is one point to note here.

64
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:58,500
Please note that the inner side and the pants are sewn together, but we have said before that we should not sew across the layer.

65
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:02,500
Here we first open the simulation to see if it is unstable.

66
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:05,500
We will see that there is some instability here.

67
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:08,500
Next, we will deal with the problem of shaking.

68
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:12,500
First of all, we need to know that the side and the pants can be sewn together.

69
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,500
These two panels are pasted together.

70
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:18,500
So here we choose the pair between the pants pocket and the pants pocket.

71
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,500
Delete by clicking Delete.

72
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:24,500
Then we sew the pocket cloth to the side of the pocket.

73
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:27,500
Remember to change the type of the pocket cloth to Turn.

74
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:32,500
After the modification, we can see that the side of the simulation is very stable.

75
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,500
There is no such shaking problem.

76
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:37,500
Finally, we put the middle piece of this piece of cloth.

77
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:40,500
Now we can see that it is actually facing the back.

78
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,500
We have to choose to turn the surface.

79
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,500
Let it face the same direction.

80
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:55,500
After completion, we finally return all the layers to the normal state.

81
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,500
That's the end of this video.

82
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,500
See you next time, bye.

